Subject: [PATCH] Assume that mod_device is global

MiuiCamera reads ro.product.mod_device and only takes the global path when
the value contains "_global". Stock spells it diting_global, ditingp_jp and
so on; this tree sets it to diting / ditingp, so the check fails and the app
goes looking for the HyperOS Security Center to put up its own permission
dialog. Nothing answers, and the camera never gets past it.

The flag it sets (Lmb/c;->E:Z) is only ever read as "is this a global build",
so force it rather than trying to spell mod_device in a way MIUI likes -
ro.product.mod_device is imported per SKU from /odm and is not ours to shape.

diff --git a/smali_classes3/mb/c.smali b/smali_classes3/mb/c.smali
--- a/smali_classes3/mb/c.smali
+++ b/smali_classes3/mb/c.smali
@@ -566,7 +566,7 @@
 
     invoke-virtual {v0, v1}, Ljava/lang/String;->contains(Ljava/lang/CharSequence;)Z
 
-    move-result v0
+    const/4 v0, 0x1
 
     sput-boolean v0, Lmb/c;->E:Z
 
